  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Terminal Signs",
    "overview": "The app is read the way an airport is read: a traveller with their hands full looks up, finds the coloured sign, reads the big number and keeps walking. Every screen carries one sign band at the top, painted in a red-to-blue gradient, (the search band on the National Dex, the identity band on a Pokémon's page). Below it, square black panel signs with light-red lettering mark every section and stick to the top while you scroll, so you always know which gate you are at: which generation among 1,025 Pokémon, or which part of a Pokémon's page.\n\nDensity is that of a departures board, not a magazine: full-bleed bands and panels, white (or sign-black) ground, firm grey rules between Dex rows, and numbers set big and extra-bold with tabular figures. Atkinson Hyperlegible Next is the single humanist signage face in four weights. The only hues outside the red-to-blue sign colors, black and grey are the 18 type colors, and every one of them always carries its type's name.\n\nThe world was chosen by the user over the category default it replaces: a grey Material list with colored type chips.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One red-to-blue gradient sign band per screen, under the status bar, holding the screen's identity in white.",
      "Square, full-width black panel signs with light-red titles head every list section and stay pinned.",
      "Big extra-bold dex numbers with tabular figures and slashed zeros.",
      "Flat: no shadows, no cards; depth comes from the gradient band against black panels against the ground.",
      "Pictograms are Material Symbols drawn in the sign's own ink.",
      "Built for one-handed, interrupted use and system font scaling up to 2.0."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Panel Edge Rule",
        "body": "Panels are sign black in light mode and panel frame in dark mode, never the ground color. A sign that disappears into the ground is not a sign.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Named Type Rule",
        "body": "A type is never shown by color alone. Every type badge prints the type's name, and matchup badges add the multiplier (\"×2\", \"×½\").",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red And Blue Is Signage Rule",
        "body": "The sign colors mark where you are and what is selected: the gradient band, the active tab, the selected game, panel titles, the top stat. The gradient only ever fills a sign band, always runs left red to right blue, and is never a fill for content or a decorative accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Per-Weight Family Rule",
        "body": "Atkinson Hyperlegible Next is loaded per weight (400, 500, 700, 800), each from its own import path, and each weight is named as its own font family. Set weight by choosing the family, never with `fontWeight` on Android, and never import the package root (it bundles all 14 files).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Big Number Rule",
        "body": "Dex numbers are four digits, extra-bold, with tabular figures, and capped at a 1.3 font-size multiplier. The number is already display size, so it stops growing before the name does; the row's number column widens with it (72 × scale, up to 1.3).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wrap First Rule",
        "body": "At large font scales text wraps onto another line rather than truncating. Sign details drop to their own line, and bands and sections grow. The one exception is the range on a Dex gate sign, which gives way first when the numeral and region need the room.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sticky Sign Rule",
        "body": "Every list section is headed by a panel sign that sticks to the top of the scroll and is replaced by the next one. On the Dex the signs are generation gates; while searching, only generations with matches get a sign, and the sign shows the match count instead of the range. On a Pokémon's page the signs are Type matchups, Abilities, Base stats, Evolution, Where to find, Moves and Pokédex entry.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Thumb Target Rule",
        "body": "Every touch target is at least 48dp, using hit slop where the visible shape is smaller: 40dp chips get 4dp above and below, the search clear button is 48dp, Back is 56dp, and rows are 56dp or taller.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Lift Rule",
        "body": "Nothing casts a shadow. A surface separates from the ground by tone and edge, never by elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Square Sign Rule",
        "body": "Anything that acts as signage (a band, a panel, a field set into a band) has square corners. Radius belongs only to marks and controls.",
        "section": "shapes"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Band Outline Rule",
        "body": "A type badge placed on the gradient band gets a 1dp white border. Off the band, badges have no border.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do give every screen one red-to-blue gradient sign band at the top (horizontal, red on the left), with white ink and the screen's title in 800-weight Atkinson Hyperlegible Next.",
      "Do head every list section with a square panel sign that sticks to the top of the scroll.",
      "Do use sign black (#0B0B0B) for panels in light mode and panel frame (#1A1A1A) in dark mode.",
      "Do print the type's name on every type badge, using its AA-checked pair from the type colors.",
      "Do outline type badges on the gradient band with 1dp white.",
      "Do set dex numbers four-digit, extra-bold and tabular, with `maxFontSizeMultiplier` 1.3.",
      "Do keep every touch target at 48dp or more, with hit slop where the visible control is smaller.",
      "Do let text wrap at large font scales and let bands, signs and rows grow; only the Dex gate range gives way first.",
      "Do load each Atkinson Hyperlegible Next weight from its own path and select weight by family.",
      "Do draw pictograms with Material Symbols in the ink of the surface they sit on."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't show a type, category or stat by color alone.",
      "Don't set a panel sign in the ground color, or round its corners.",
      "Don't add shadows or elevation; separate surfaces by tone and edge.",
      "Don't use the sign gradient or sign red as a content fill or decoration; they mark place and selection only.",
      "Don't add hues beyond the sign red, blue and panel red, black, the greys and the 18 type colors.",
      "Don't use `fontWeight` to pick an Atkinson weight on Android, or import the font package root.",
      "Don't truncate names, details or labels at large font scale when they can wrap."
    ]
  }
}
